= Weekend & Holiday Travel Policies

== Business Travel Across Weekends

Employees are ordinarily expected to travel on standard business days. Expenses incurred over weekends or public holidays are subject to heightened scrutiny and verification.

#policy-rule("POL-WKD-001", "Weekend Expense Eligibility")[
  Expenses incurred on Saturdays, Sundays, or declared statutory holidays are eligible for reimbursement only if:
  - The employee is conducting approved client engagements, trade shows, or official corporate events on that specific calendar day, or
  - Departure on Sunday is required to attend a mandatory Monday morning business meeting scheduled prior to 10:00 AM local time where Sunday night lodging is demonstrably necessary.
]

== Combining Business Travel with Personal Leisure (Bleisure)

Employees may extend business travel for personal leisure at their own expense, provided there is zero incremental cost to the company.

#policy-rule("POL-WKD-002", "Personal Leisure Cost Neutrality")[
  Any hotel nights, meals, car rental days, or local transit incurred during personal extension days must be paid directly by the employee. If extending a trip increases round-trip airfare, the employee must provide a price quote of the direct business-only itinerary and reimburse the company for any price difference.
]

#policy-warning("POL-WKD-003", "Non-Reimbursable Weekend Sightseeing")[
  Sightseeing tours, admission tickets to museums, sporting events, recreational equipment rentals, and leisure excursions incurred over weekends or during personal extensions are strictly non-reimbursable.
]
